# Line endings are a correctness concern in this project, not a style one.
#
# The pipeline's whole verdict rests on byte-exact patch application: a model's
# patch is judged by whether `git apply` accepts it and whether the result equals
# the intended file. Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# the working tree to CRLF on checkout. Without this file, that conversion:
#
#   1. breaks every hash-verified blob in data/file_cache (the content no longer
#      hashes to its own filename, so every lookup is a cache miss — which silently
#      collapses the token projection and makes a sweep run zero cells), and
#   2. turns the jsdiff -> git apply gate red, because an LF patch applies and then
#      reads back as CRLF. `doctor` reports "the patch applied but the result does
#      not equal the intended file".
#
# The same hazard corrupted the Phase-1 results of the Python study, which is why
# that project refuses to run on native Windows at all. Here it is fixed rather
# than refused.
#
# Working-tree form is LF everywhere. Binary and content-addressed files are
# excluded from conversion entirely.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ──────────────────────────── content-addressed: never convert, never diff
# These are byte-exact artefacts whose filename IS their SHA-256. Any conversion
# invalidates them. `-text` disables eol translation on both directions.
data/file_cache/blobs/**        -text
recovery-bench/data/file_cache/blobs/**  -text
recovery-bench/archive/SHA256SUMS        -text

# Frozen dataset: revision-pinned and hash-checked on load.
recovery-bench/data/swebench_lite.jsonl  -text

# ──────────────────────────── binaries
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.docx    binary
*.pptx    binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.zip     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ico     binary

# ──────────────────────────── scripts that must stay LF to run under bash/WSL
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf

# Lockfiles: text, but never worth diffing in review.
bun.lock           text eol=lf -diff
recovery-bench/bun.lock  text eol=lf -diff
